Subject: [PATCH] J714s release 6: kernel v272-11 (fans, fast-die limit,
 RFCOMM, dock fixes) and hyprland-m5 0.57.2-3

Re-pinned from betizzel/omarchy-m5 ee5df84: linux-aurora
7.3.0.aurora17.v272-11 (c2fdaa24..., 44227182 bytes): aurora-silicon/linux
integration/aurora a5ebec5f plus patches/j714s-27.2/linux 0001-0032
(v272-7 plus Isaac-Duarte's J714s fan targets #1944 and dock tunnel fix
#1930, DjDeveloperr's SN201202x LDCM fix #1721 and J714s fast-die limit
#1950, Jens Axboe's PMP power domains through s2idle #1789, three G17
fixes merged upstream, and BT_RFCOMM / PKCS8_PRIVATE_KEY_PARSER).
The qualification pins follow 7.3.0-17.v272-11-ARCH.

hyprland-m5 0.57.2-3 from 41d8d77 (the latch members moved to the end of
CMonitor so stock-built plugins keep their offsets, betizzel/omarchy-m5#8):
the package built on the J714s (.pkg.tar.xz, sha256 531fc814...) recompressed
to zstd; the tar inside is the same (sha256 62c59415...), c87f2570...,
51124129 bytes. Nothing else changes. Set j714s-dev-runtime-c4fe82ac5a13.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
